            <ArticleTitle>Application of CRISPR-Cas system in gene therapy: Pre-clinical progress in animal model.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1568-7864(16)30176-8</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.dnarep.2016.07.004</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The clustered regularly interspaced short palindromic repeats (CRISPRs) and their associated proteins (Cas) belong to the crucial adaptive immune system, which exist in archaea and bacteria. Currently, CRISPR-Cas9 system has been modified and widely used to edit genome. In this review, we summarized the discovery, classification and mechanism of CRISPR-Cas system and further discussed the application of CRISPR-Cas9 in gene therapy, mainly in disease models.</AbstractText>
